Z||000003||Pyric||12-04-2001||10:32 AM||||I've seen those scoops with either one hole or 2 (side by side).  If you are going with 2 then you can get the honeycomb-like mesh from the underside of the louvered deck vents off an early model Fiero (because it wont be enough to cover a single hole.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Otherwise go to:<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.nopionline.com/universalparts.asp?Level1=Custom%20Exterior&Level2=Grille%20Mesh&Level3=APC&Level4=&Level5=" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nopionline.com/universalparts.asp?Level1=Custo m%20Exterior&Level2=Grille%20Mesh&Level3=APC&Level4=&Level5=</A> <P>They have universal grill mesh.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||12-04-2001||10:36 AM||||Go to your local Home Depot type store and look at the wire screens for keeping leaves out of house eavestroughing.  It's kind of diamond shaped and pressed, which makes it good lookin and strong.  Other alternatives are wire waste baskets or racks and baskets for cooking utensils.  Look in a cooking equipment store.  If you have a demolition/salvage place in town they usually have all sorts of cool stuff.<P>Gary||||reg||7
Z||000005||Dumba$$||12-04-2001||11:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroBUZZ:<BR><B>Go to your local Home Depot type store and look at the wire screens for keeping leaves out of house eavestroughing.  It's kind of diamond shaped and pressed, which makes it good lookin and strong.  Other alternatives are wire waste baskets or racks and baskets for cooking utensils.  Look in a cooking equipment store.  If you have a demolition/salvage place in town they usually have all sorts of cool stuff.<P>Gary</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i agree with you<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||jimmybpei||12-04-2001||12:54 PM||||Teh mess tha pyric is talking about would be best, 'cause it would retain the factory look. Only because that honycomb is synonomouse with Pontiac. What i used for my hood was the mesh from an old 5 foot satelite dish only because the honeycomb wasnt big enough.<P>Later<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jimmybpeisig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
